{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And made</b>: There is a distinction in <b>between</b> with a mem [following], as in <b>between</b> waters and waters (Genesis 1:6), <b>between</b> sacred and profane (Ezekiel 44:23). And there is [usage] with <b>between</b> and <b>between</b>, as here: \"and he separated <b>between</b> the waters that were below the expanse and <b>between</b> the waters,\" etc. And there is [usage] with both, as in \"<b>between</b> you and <b>between</b> your Elohim\" (Isaiah 8:19 [in some enumerations])." "<b>And the meaning of \"and it was so\"</b> is joined to what follows it: as it was so, he called them shamayim."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:30.680585821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}